<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/63fea9965a9c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Algorithmic Defamation: The Case of the Shameless Autocomplete" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/66ab12b4fc9e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "For instance, querying Bing for “Torchmark” returns as the second suggestion, “torchmark corporation job scam.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/694b5fb75ec0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Australian to sue Google for defamation over search results" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "679" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/72046bf410f1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "And I used a list of U.S. congresspeople from the Sunlight Foundation to query for each person’s first and last name, as well as adding either “representative” or “senator” before their name." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/720554985e80> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The case involved someone who was upset that doing a Google search on his name popped up \"con man\" (\"truffatore\") and \"fraud\" (\"truffa\") as autocomplete Google search suggestions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "684" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/80b84f23f771> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Berkman Center’s Digital Media Law Project (DMLP) defines a defamatory statement generally as, “a false statement of fact that exposes a person to hatred, ridicule or contempt, lowers him in the esteem of his peers, causes him to be shunned, or injures him in his business or trade.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8bce3fe64601> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google search reveals names of rape victims" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6487" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9194d9dc899d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "There are other cases that may be more clear-cut instances of defamation, such as on Bing “Joe Barton” suggesting “joe barton scam” which was not corrected when adding the title “representative” to the front of the query." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9ada93c9d5d7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "People searching via Google for Piana's client, who remains publicly unnamed, were apparently presented with autocomplete suggestions including truffatore ('con man') and truffa ('fraud')." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "676" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9f97dd15886d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His Honour Justice Blue reasoned that the defamatory phrase was 'generated by Google programs as a result of Google's programming'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8f3a4fff30f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google's auto-complete and related search functions are revealing the identity of rape victims who have been granted anonymity." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6487" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ab4180026557> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google's auto-complete and related search functions are revealing the identity of rape victims who have been granted anonymity." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6487" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/abfbea01ab54> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google held to be a publisher of defamatory autocomplete and related search terms" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ae2e9bbac400> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Tuesday, lead counsel Carlo Piana wrote on his blog that the Court of Milan has upheld its earlier decision to order Google to filter out libellous search suggestions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "676" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b2657830383b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "For instance, querying Bing for “Torchmark” returns as the second suggestion, “torchmark corporation job scam.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b6fa856deb51> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Trkulja is also claiming defamation around Google's \"autocomplete\" options for his name, which have included phrases like \"is a former hit man,\" ''criminal\" and \"underworld.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "679" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c2ae9ad6b5e4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Tuesday, lead counsel Carlo Piana wrote on his blog that the Court of Milan has upheld its earlier decision to order Google to filter out libellous search suggestions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "676" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe9c5a7a1c0b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "So when you Google for “Gerald Connolly” one suggestion that comes up is “gerald connolly armed robbery,” not because Congressman Gerald Connolly robbed anyone but because someone else in Canada by the same name did." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/feda9016c3df> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google Found Liable For Autocomplete Suggestions In Italy" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "684" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Risk/9d7689cf3670> a airo:Risk ;
    rdfs:label "Risk of defamation through AI-generated search suggestions" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.9"^^xsd:float ;
