<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1fff6318c24c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "So when you Google for “Gerald Connolly” one suggestion that comes up is “gerald connolly armed robbery,” not because Congressman Gerald Connolly robbed anyone but because someone else in Canada by the same name did." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/be3851616487> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The South Australian Supreme Court has found that Google published defamatory statements that appeared in autocomplete and related search terms on its search engine." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f87fd3e6f74f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google lost its bid to claim the protection of the E-Commerce Directive's safe harbour provisions, which partly shields hosting and ISPs from liability for content held on or transmitted over their systems." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "676" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fc7d79621242> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Germany's former first lady, Bettina Wulff, had commenced a similar action, which had been stayed, pending the outcome in today’s case." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "683" .

