<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/078cb8fcd8fe> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Germany’s former first lady, Bettina Wulff, had commenced a similar action, which had been stayed, pending the outcome in today’s case." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "683" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3c374408d6ea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His Honour decided that there was no reason why Google should not be held accountable for these 'publications' after it was put on notice by the plaintiff." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7a0a3b9b9977> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "4 years later, the Victorian Court of Appeal overturned the decision, finding the case had no prospect of successfully proving defamation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "679" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9a73f9a9768a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Milorad \"Michael\" Trkulja was shot in the back in 2004 in a restaurant in Melbourne, Australia's second largest city." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "679" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c16d59904abd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His Honour Justice Blue reasoned that the defamatory phrase was 'generated by Google programs as a result of Google's programming'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e128034ea35e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Australian High Court unanimously ruled in favor of Trkulja, supporting his allegation that a Google search of his name could indicate to an ordinary person he was \"somehow associated with the Melbourne criminal underworld.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "679" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fbec2bcaf9ce> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Court of Appeals (Oberlandesgericht) Köln had found, in the previous instance, in favour of Google." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "683" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fd943aee104c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rape charity, The Survivors Trust, told the Times it was \"beyond shocking\" that Google's search engine threw up the names of victims." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6487" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/13e128a2a3d4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In Germany, a man recently won a legal battle with Google over the fact that when you searched for his name, the autocomplete suggestions connected him to “scientology” and “fraud,” — two things that he felt had defamatory insinuations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5dbca846d086> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Trkulja had successfully argued in the Victoria state Supreme Court in 2012 that Google defamed him by publishing photos of him linked to hardened criminals of Melbourne's underworld." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "679" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6056e0fbf03d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His Honour Justice Blue also followed the reasoning of the Victorian Supreme Court in Trkulja v Google Inc LLC (No 5) and held that Google was the publisher of defamatory search results." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7b3b10cab3bf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Technically, the claimants’ right to request Google to cease and desist is based on Sec. 823, 1004 German Civil Code (BGB) and Art. 1, 2, Basic Law (Grundgesetz)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "683" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3fd30f2a1fbe> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The South Australian Supreme Court has found that Google published defamatory statements that appeared in autocomplete and related search terms on its search engine." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8a93a03c121a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "I automatically collected data on both Google and Bing autocompletions for a number of different queries relating to public companies and politicians." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "674" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a6c9b225cb1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This morning, the Federal Supreme Court (Bundesgerichtshof) has held Google liable for a functionality of its search engine, the autocomplete function." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "683" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0f5826e41426> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Tuesday, lead counsel Carlo Piana wrote on his blog that the Court of Milan has upheld its earlier decision to order Google to filter out libellous search suggestions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "676" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e9f9e2acff91> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google said it had removed all examples it had been \"made aware of\"." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6487" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f925f0284d9f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Here's yet another ridiculously bad ruling for search engines in Italy. Glyn Moody points us to the news of a blog post by a lawyer involved in the case (against Google) who is happy that his side prevailed and that Google is liable for search autocomplete suggestions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "684" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dbd3402341a5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In his judgment, his Honour referred to the 'only authority' on this point as supporting this conclusion, being the decision of the High Court of Hong Kong in Dr Yeung Sau Shing Albert v Google Inc." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "685" .

